  "body": "## What changed\n\nSecond slice of #3919, and all of #4239.\n\n- **Shrink-fit chucks** (`crates/tools/src/holder_library_shrink.rs`). The library gets DIN 69882-8 shrink-fit chucks on each taper except TTS: BT30, BT40, CAT40, SK30, SK40, ISO30, HSK-A63, HSK-F63, HSK-E40, HSK-E32, BT50 and CAT50 (127 entries, \"BT40 Shrink 12 mm\").\n  - A new clamp kind: `Clamp::Shrink { bore, nose_d, body_d }`.\n  - The outline is one envelope: the 4.5-degree nose cone from d2 to d3, under the 45-degree flare from the flange front. At each height the larger of the two is drawn. A short chuck is drawn whole and is not refused.\n  - The nose and the body are drawn 2 mm wider in radius than the table (`SHRINK_MARGIN`). Reason: one maker's chuck of the same size is 1.53 mm wider.\n- **BT50 and CAT50** (`crates/tools/src/holder_library_fifty.rs`). Each taper gets ER16-ER40 and each Weldon bore, with a default gauge length of 100.\n- **Picker.** One grouped \"<taper> Shrink\" row for each taper, the same as \"<taper> Weldon\" (#2018). It resolves to the bore that takes the tool's shank (`shrink_for`). An unknown bore is refused by name.\n- **#4239.** `SPINDLE_MOUNTS` now lists each library taper (13 names). The app test `every_library_taper_is_a_spindle_mount` keeps the two lists equal. It also loads each library holder in its own mount. An unknown mount (\"HSK-A100\", \"HSK-A99\", \"R8\") is still refused by name.\n- The UI clamp texts, the MCP `list_holder_library` output (`\"kind\": \"Shrink\"`) and the tool descriptions (with `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md`) know the new kind.\n- `LibraryError` moved to `holder_library_error.rs`, and the Weldon bore tables moved to `holder_library_weldon.rs`. This keeps `holder_library.rs` under 400 lines (388).\n- Each number and its source: `docs/decisions/3919-standard-holders-2.md`. We did not copy a vendor model.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `holder_library::shrink::tests::*`: the recorded rows, the listed entries, the SK40 12 mm and BT40 6 mm outlines point by point, never under the table steel (each entry, default and shortest gauge), a wider maker's chuck stays inside, the grouped picker and its refusal, the envelope edge cases.\n- `holder_library::fifty::tests::*`: the BT50 / CAT50 table, the entries, the BT50 ER32 outline, the CAT50 flange position.\n- `machine::tooling::tests::the_new_library_tapers_are_spindle_mounts` (post).\n- `machine_default_holder::every_library_taper_is_a_spindle_mount` (app).\n- Updated: `holder_library::tests::*`, `holder_library::weldon::tests::*`, and the din / hsk tests now count only the ER and Weldon entries.\n\n## Gate (winbuild, Windows; head 9921f2961)\n\nDefault job count (full parallelism). Log `C:\\camcraft-logs\\gate-3919c-9921f2961.log` (the head SHA is on its first line).\n\n| Step | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-tools --lib` | ok, 214 passed (all `shrink::tests` and `fifty::tests` included) |\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-post --lib` | ok, 161 passed (`the_new_library_tapers_are_spindle_mounts` included) |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` | ok |\n| `camcraft-app` lib | ok, 318 passed |\n| `camcraft-app` `holder_library` | ok, 12 passed |\n| `camcraft-app` `holder_reference` | ok, 7 passed |\n| `camcraft-app` `machine_default_holder` | ok, 14 passed (`every_library_taper_is_a_spindle_mount` included) |\n| `camcraft-app` `mcp_doc_drift` | ok, 9 passed |\n| `camcraft-app` `mcp_holder` | ok, 5 passed |\n| `camcraft-ui` lib, filter `tool_holder tool_library_holders` | ok, 12 passed |\n\nAn earlier run on head 32a373698 did not compile (a borrow in the grouped picker loop). Commit 9921f2961 fixes it. The `cargo xtask gate quick --base <#4240 branch> --dry-run` plan of that run had 130 steps.\n\nThe quick plan against the base branch reaches many `camcraft-app` test binaries, because `crates/app/src/mcp/` changed. winbuild stalls when it links the whole set. For this reason the run has the tools and post steps and the named app and UI holder suites only, the same as #4240. The full app quick plan was not run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full `camcraft-app` quick plan, and the UI suites other than the `tool_holder` / `tool_library_holders` filter.\n- The light lane, and the example catalog suites (no post or toolpath changed).\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill row of `list_holder_library` still names only the first tapers. It is a process file, so this PR does not change it.\n\n## Left out (decision file)\n\n- CAT30: the sources do not agree on the flange diameter, and no source gives the flange thickness.\n- Inch shrink-fit bores: the inch tables give a different nose and body for the same bore at each length.\n- SK50, Morse, NMTB, hydraulic and milling chucks, ER50, TG and SF32 are for later slices. SF32 waits for the owner's measurements.\n\nChangelog: Holder library: DIN 69882-8 shrink-fit chucks on each taper but TTS (one grouped \"<taper> Shrink\" pick), BT50 and CAT50 holders with ER and Weldon noses; a machine file can state each holder library taper as `tooling.spindle_mount` (#3919, #4239)\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #3919\nFixes #4239\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe screens come from the UI test harness. The test code is the same for both states. It is not part of the PR.\n\nHolder picker. The Library holder list of the tool library window is open. The pointer is on the BT40 row. The tooltip shows the row text.\n\nBefore (main): the BT40 row is \"Weldon\". There is no shrink-fit row.\n\n![Before: holder picker](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4251/before-holder-picker.png)\n\nAfter (this PR): the new \"BT40 Shrink\" row is in the list. Its tooltip says \"shrink fit\" and lists the bores.\n\n![After: holder picker](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4251/after-holder-picker.png)\n\nHolders page of the tool library window. The filter is \"BT40\". The Clamp column shows the clamp of each holder.\n\nBefore (main): the BT40 rows are ER collets and Weldon side locks only.\n\n![Before: Holders page](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4251/before-holders-page.png)\n\nAfter (this PR): the BT40 Shrink rows show \"shrink fit\" in the Clamp column.\n\n![After: Holders page](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4251/after-holders-page.png)\n\n",
